window.AG_CHAPTERS["10"] = {"id":"10","title":"Old Wu, One Winter Later","titleZh":"吳伯，又一個冬天","patient":{"name":"Old Wu 吳伯","sprite":"man"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-clinic.jpg","key":"river"},"pattern":"Kidney Yang Deficiency 腎陽虛","principle":"warm and tonify Kidney yang, and rebuild the root of the fire","tongue":"pale and swollen, moist, with a white coating","pulseNote":{"en":"You have to press to find it, and when you do it comes slowly and without strength — weakest of all at the deep, rearmost position.","zh":"沉取始得，遲而無力，尤以尺部為弱"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>T&#224;ix&#299; KI3</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"KI3","zh":"太谿","py":"T&#224;ix&#299;","x":113,"y":868,"img":"art/body-leg-medial.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":0,"y":560,"w":434,"h":599},"decoys":[{"x":178,"y":722},{"x":196,"y":900},{"x":325,"y":966},{"x":152,"y":876},{"x":88,"y":762}],"note":"<b>太谿 T&#224;ix&#299; KI3</b> — in the depression between the tip of the medial malleolus and the Achilles tendon, level with the tip of the malleolus. Source point and Stream point of the Kidney; it treats both Kidney yin and Kidney yang.<br>內踝尖與跟腱之間凹陷處，與內踝尖平齊。腎經原穴、輸穴，陰陽俱調。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"Cold is only the beginning of the question. Ask <b>where</b> he is cold, <b>when</b> he is worst, and what his water and his stool are doing.","zh":"寒僅為問之始。當問：冷在何處？何時最甚？小便大便如何？"},"look":{"en":"A pale tongue you have seen. Look also at how <b>wet</b> it is — fluids that are not being moved sit on the surface.","zh":"舌淡已見過。更當觀其潤否——水津不化，則停於舌面。"},"pulse":{"en":"Press deep. And pay attention to the <b>rear</b> position under your ring finger — that is where the Kidney answers.","zh":"當沉取。且留意無名指下之尺部——腎脈應於此。"},"dx":{"en":"First decide whether this cold is <b>full</b> or <b>empty</b>. Then find whose yang it is. Then say how yang deficiency differs from plain qi deficiency.","zh":"先辨其寒為實為虛。次求其陽虛在何臟。末辨陽虛與氣虛之異。"},"rx":{"en":"The Source point of a channel treats the organ itself. And do not forget that the acquired root can be used to feed the innate one.","zh":"原穴主本臟。且勿忘後天可養先天。"},"tech":{"en":"Of all the patterns you have met, this is the one that asks for fire.","zh":"歷來諸證，唯此證非火不可。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen recognises him before he speaks. \"The dawn crossing. It has been three years.\"","zh":"參師父在他開口前就認出來了。「早渡的。三年了。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"Old Wu keeps both hands inside his sleeves, even by the brazier.","zh":"吳伯雙手一直籠在袖子裡，就算坐在火盆邊也是。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy sets the tea down and Old Wu holds the cup rather than drinking it.","zh":"藥童把茶擱下，吳伯只是捧著，並不喝。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"You treated his knees once with warmth and it worked. Do not assume it is the same illness.\"","zh":"「你曾以溫法治其膝而效。莫以為仍是舊病。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"It's not the knees this time,\" he says. \"It's that I can't get warm from the inside any more.\"","zh":"「這回不是膝蓋，」他說，「是從裡頭暖不起來了。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"Listen to that sentence. He has told you where the fire has gone out.\"","zh":"「聽這句話。他已經告訴你火滅在哪裡了。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"cold_heat","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"cold_heat"},"reward":{"cardEn":"Warm the Root","cardZh":"溫補腎陽","cardTxt":"Cold that comes from outside is driven out. Cold that comes from an empty hearth is not driven anywhere — it is answered by rebuilding the fire. Warm and tonify together; warming alone consumes what little yang remains.","herbId":"renshen","herbEn":"Ginseng","herbZh":"人參","herbImg":"art/card-renshen.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Sweet, slightly bitter and slightly warm; in TCM it is the great tonifier of original qi. In a yang-deficient formula it is paired with genuinely warming herbs — it restores the strength behind the fire rather than supplying the fire itself. Ginseng is strong medicine and is prescribed by a qualified practitioner, not taken casually."},"endings":{"three":["At the spring festival Old Wu poles the first crossing of the day again, sleeves rolled up. \"I sleep till light now,\" he says. \"And I'm warm in my own bed.\"<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You have finished the road. Ten patients ago you could not tell cold from heat. Today you told empty cold from full cold, found whose yang had failed, and knew that this — of all the empty patterns — was the one that wanted fire.\"<br><br>He hands you a needle case.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"The grove has a physician in it again.\"","春社那天，吳伯又撐了當日第一班渡，袖子捲得高高的。「現在能睡到天亮，」他說，「被窩裡自己就是暖的。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「路你走完了。十個病人以前，你連寒熱都分不清。今日你能於寒中分虛實，於陽虛中定其臟，且知諸虛之中，唯此一證需火。」<br><br>他遞給你一個針囊。<br><b>參師父：</b>「杏林裡，又有大夫了。」"],"two":["He is warmer and sleeps longer, but still wakes before dawn to the privy.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You warmed him. You did not quite finish rebuilding the fire that keeps him warm without you.\"","他暖和些了，也睡得長些，仍是天未亮就得起。<br><b>參師父：</b>「你溫了他。那把離了你也能自暖的火，你還沒有築完。」"],"one":["He is no warmer. The dawn crossing still goes without him.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Cold, yes. But you never asked whether it came from outside or from an empty hearth. Those two want opposite treatments.\"","他還是暖不起來。早渡仍舊沒有他。<br><b>參師父：</b>「寒，不錯。然你未問此寒是自外來，抑或爐中無火。二者治法相反。」"],"titles":["Old Wu Takes the Dawn Crossing","Old Wu Sleeps Longer","Old Wu Will Need Another Visit"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Your last patient. You treated this man three winters ago — cold and damp lodged in his knees. He got better.","cn":"你最後一位病人。三年前你治過他——寒濕痹阻於膝，後來好了。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. It's Wu. The knees have been quiet since. This is something else, and it's been coming on slowly.","cn":"大夫。姓吳。膝蓋自那以後就安靜了。這回是別的，來得慢。"},{"w":"patient","en":"I'm cold all the time now. Low back and knees, sore and cold together. And I've no strength for the pole.","cn":"現在整天怕冷。腰和膝又酸又冷。撐篙也沒力氣了。"},{"w":"master","en":"Three years ago the cold was on the outside, sitting in his channels. Ask yourself whether that is still true.","cn":"三年前那寒在外，客於經絡。你當自問：如今是否仍然如此。"},{"w":"master","en":"A man can be cold because winter got into him. A man can also be cold because his own fire has burned low. They look alike from across the room.","cn":"人之寒，或因冬入於身，或因己火將熄。隔室觀之，二者無別。"}],"qa":[{"q":"Where exactly are you cold, and does anything make it better?","cq":"具體冷在哪裡？什麼情況會好一些？","good":1,"a":"Low back and knees most of all, and my feet. Warmth helps while it lasts, then it goes again.","ca":"最冷是腰、膝，還有腳。烤火時舒服，離了火又冷回去。","clue":{"en":"Cold and sore low back and knees, relieved by warmth","zh":"腰膝冷痛、得溫則減"},"note":"Location decides the organ. The low back is the house of the Kidney and the knees are governed by it; cold and soreness there together, rather than in a joint that was injured, points at the Kidney rather than at a channel. That warmth helps only while it is applied says the fire is not being made inside. 部位定臟。腰為腎之府，膝為腎所主。腰膝冷而兼酸，非傷處一節之痛，故病在腎不在經。得溫則暫舒，離之即復，明其火不能自生。"},{"q":"How is your urine, especially at night?","cq":"小便如何？夜裡尤其怎樣？","good":1,"a":"Clear as water, and a lot of it. I'm up three or four times a night.","ca":"清如水，量還多。夜裡要起三四回。","clue":{"en":"Copious clear urine, frequent at night","zh":"小便清長、夜尿頻多"},"note":"<b>The Kidney's own signature.</b> The Kidney governs water and holds it; when its yang is too weak to warm and contain, fluid passes through unchanged — clear, copious, and worst at night when yang is naturally at its lowest. Dark scanty urine would mean the opposite. 此腎自身之徵。腎主水而司開闔，陽虛不能溫攝，則水直下而不化，故清長；夜為陽衰之時，故夜尿尤多。小便短赤者反是。"},{"q":"What time of day do you open your bowels, and what are the stools like?","cq":"大便在什麼時辰？形狀如何？","good":1,"a":"Just before dawn, every day, loose and urgent. It wakes me.","ca":"每天天亮前，稀而急，把我催醒。","clue":{"en":"Dawn diarrhoea, loose and urgent","zh":"五更瀉"},"note":"Dawn diarrhoea — <b>五更瀉</b>. The hours before sunrise are when yang is thinnest; a Kidney yang too weak to warm the Spleen lets the bowel loosen exactly then, and only then. It is one of the most specific findings in the whole of pattern differentiation, and it is why this case is the Kidney and not simply the Spleen. 五更瀉。黎明陽氣最微，腎陽不能溫脾，故獨於此時而瀉。此為辨證中最具特異性之症，亦本案屬腎而非單屬脾之所憑。"},{"q":"Has your spirit or your drive changed?","cq":"精神、心氣有變化嗎？","good":1,"a":"I sit by the brazier and don't want to move. Not sad exactly. Just banked down, like a fire covered over.","ca":"整天坐在火盆邊不想動。也不是難過，就是壓著一層灰，火燒不旺。","clue":{"en":"Listlessness, withdrawal, low drive","zh":"精神萎靡、但欲寐"},"note":"Worth asking, and the image he reaches for is the right one. Yang is warmth, movement and drive. When it is short a person does not become sorrowful so much as banked — quiet, still, wanting to sleep. This is not the same as low mood from a constrained Liver, which is restless rather than still. 問得有據，其譬亦切。陽者，溫煦、動、志之所本。陽虛者非哀，乃如火覆灰——靜、少動、但欲寐。與肝鬱之情志不舒不同：彼躁而此靜。"},{"q":"Do you have a fever, and is there thirst for cold drinks?","cq":"發熱嗎？口渴喜冷飲嗎？","good":0,"a":"No fever. I drink hot water all day, and not much of it.","ca":"不發熱。整天喝熱水，也喝得不多。","clue":"","note":"A correct exclusion. Preference for hot drinks and little thirst confirms cold rather than heat, and rules out the phlegm-heat and yin-deficient patterns you have already met. 排除得當。喜熱飲而不甚渴，主寒不主熱，且可排除前所見之痰熱與陰虛二證。"}],"look":[{"t":"Pale and swollen, moist, with a white coating","c":"舌淡胖而潤、苔白","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Pale swollen moist tongue, white coat","zh":"舌淡胖潤、苔白"},"note":"Correct. Pale = yang is not warming the blood up to the surface. Swollen and <b>wet</b> = fluids are not being transformed, so they pool. White coat = cold. The wetness is what separates this from the last patient: hers was pale and swollen too, but not sodden. 是。淡者陽不溫運血上榮；胖而潤者水津不化而停聚；苔白者寒。潤之一字，即與前案之別：彼亦淡胖，然不至於水滑。"},{"t":"Pale body with a thin white coat, normal moisture","c":"舌淡苔薄白，潤度如常","ok":0,"note":"That is qi or blood deficiency without the water backing up. Close, but it misses the swelling and the wetness, which are what tell you yang — not merely qi — has failed. 此為氣虛或血虛而水未停。相近，然漏其胖與潤，而此二者正示陽虛而非徒氣虛。"},{"t":"Red body with little coating","c":"舌紅少苔","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat — the opposite pole of the same axis. Everything in this case is cold and wet. 陰虛內熱之象，與本案同軸而反極。本案通身寒而水停。"},{"t":"Pale body with a white greasy coat","c":"舌淡、苔白膩","ok":0,"note":"Cold-damp, which is close and worth considering, especially in a man who works on the river. But a greasy coat means damp with substance sitting in the middle; his coat is thin and simply wet. 寒濕之象，於長年在河上者尤當一慮。然苔膩者中焦有形之濕；本案苔薄而但潤耳。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Deep, slow and weak, especially at the rear position 沉遲無力，尺尤弱","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Deep slow weak pulse, weak at the chi position","zh":"脈沉遲無力、尺弱"},"note":"Correct, and every word of it is load-bearing. <b>Deep</b>: the disease is interior. <b>Slow</b>: cold. <b>Weak</b>: deficiency, not excess. And the <b>rear (chi) position</b> under the ring finger is where the Kidney answers — its particular weakness names the organ. Deep and slow but <i>forceful</i> would be full cold instead. 是，字字有據。沉主裡，遲主寒，無力主虛。尺部候腎，其獨弱者，正所以定臟。若沉遲而有力，則為實寒矣。"},{"t":"Deep, slow and forceful 沉遲有力","ok":0,"note":"That is <b>full</b> cold — cold congealing in the interior, which is drained and warmed, not tonified. The one word that separates the two treatments is \"forceful\". 此為實寒，寒凝於裡，當溫散而不當補。二治之別，只在「有力」二字。"},{"t":"Thready and rapid 細數","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat. Same axis, opposite end. Nothing here is fast and nothing here is hot. 陰虛內熱之脈。同軸而反極。本案無數無熱。"},{"t":"Floating and tight 浮緊","ok":0,"note":"Exterior wind-cold — chapter one. That pulse belongs to an illness three days old. His has been coming on for a year. 風寒表證，第一章之脈。彼病三日，此病經年。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — is this cold full, or empty?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：此寒為實寒，抑或虛寒？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Empty cold — cold arising because yang is insufficient","c":"虛寒 — 陽虛而生內寒","ok":1,"note":"<b>The whole case turns here.</b> Full cold is an <i>invasion</i>: sudden onset, severe fixed pain, aversion to cold with a forceful pulse, and the patient is otherwise strong. Empty cold is a <i>failure</i>: gradual onset over months, cold that is sore rather than sharp, relieved by warmth and by pressure, listlessness, and a pulse without force. Old Wu is the second, in every particular. Full cold is driven out; empty cold is rebuilt. 一案之樞在此。實寒者，邪之犯也：驟起、痛劇而有定處、惡寒而脈有力，其人本不虛。虛寒者，陽之衰也：漸起經月、冷而酸不劇、得溫得按則減、精神萎靡、脈無力。吳伯處處屬後者。實寒當散，虛寒當補。"},{"t":"Full cold — cold congealing in the channels","c":"實寒 — 寒凝經絡","ok":0,"note":"That was his illness three winters ago, and you treated it correctly then. But that came on suddenly with fixed severe pain and a forceful pulse. This has come on over a year, his pulse has no force, and the cold eases when you press. 此乃三年前之病，爾時所治不誤。然彼驟起、痛有定處而劇、脈有力。今則經年漸來、脈無力、按之則舒。"},{"t":"Cold-damp obstructing the channels","c":"寒濕痹阻經絡","ok":0,"note":"The same trap, wearing a coat. A bi pattern hurts in joints, is worse in wet weather and does not produce clear copious urine or dawn diarrhoea. Those two findings are organ findings, not channel findings. 同一陷阱，換一件衣裳。痹證痛在關節，遇陰雨加重，不見小便清長與五更瀉。此二症屬臟不屬經。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — whose yang has failed?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：陽虛在何臟？</small>","opts":[{"t":"The Kidney &mdash; and the Spleen is cold because of it","c":"腎陽虛 — 脾寒因之而起","ok":1,"note":"Three findings name the Kidney and no other organ: <b>cold sore low back and knees</b> (the Kidney's house and the joint it governs), <b>clear copious urine with nocturia</b> (the Kidney governs water), and <b>dawn diarrhoea</b> (Kidney yang failing to warm the Spleen at the hour yang is thinnest). The weakest pulse at the chi position confirms it. Spleen yang deficiency alone would give loose stool at any hour and no urinary sign at all. 三症獨指於腎：腰膝冷酸（腰為腎府，膝為腎所主）、小便清長夜尿（腎主水）、五更瀉（陽微之時，腎不溫脾）。尺脈獨弱，益以為證。單純脾陽虛者，瀉不擇時，且無小便之症。"},{"t":"The Spleen alone","c":"單為脾陽虛","ok":0,"note":"Then why is the low back cold, why is he up four times a night, and why does the diarrhoea keep to one hour of the day? The Spleen governs none of those three. 若單為脾陽虛，則腰何以冷？夜何以四起？瀉何以獨在一時？此三者皆非脾所主。"},{"t":"The Heart","c":"心陽虛","ok":0,"note":"Heart yang deficiency brings palpitations, chest oppression, cold limbs and a knotted or intermittent pulse. He has no chest complaint at all, and his pulse is slow and weak rather than irregular. 心陽虛當見心悸、胸悶、四肢厥冷、脈結代。本案胸中無事，脈遲弱而不結代。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — and how does yang deficiency differ from plain qi deficiency?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：陽虛與氣虛何別？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Yang deficiency is qi deficiency plus cold","c":"陽虛者，氣虛而兼寒象","ok":1,"note":"The cleanest rule in the whole of pattern differentiation, and the right note to finish on. <b>Qi deficiency:</b> fatigue, shortness of breath, spontaneous sweating, weak pulse — a shortage of <i>function</i>, with no temperature to it. <b>Yang deficiency:</b> all of that, <i>plus</i> cold — aversion to cold, cold limbs, cold that eases with warmth, clear urine, a pale wet tongue, a slow pulse. Yang is qi with warmth in it; lose the warmth and qi deficiency becomes yang deficiency. That is also why this pattern, alone among the empty ones, asks for moxa. 辨證中最簡明之則，亦以此收筆。氣虛者：倦怠、氣短、自汗、脈弱——功能之不足，而無寒熱之偏。陽虛者：兼具上述，而更見寒象——畏寒、肢冷、得溫則減、小便清長、舌淡而潤、脈遲。陽者，氣之溫者也；失其溫，則氣虛轉為陽虛。此亦諸虛之中，獨此證宜灸之故。"},{"t":"They are the same thing described in two ways","c":"二者名異而實同","ok":0,"note":"Then you would treat them the same way, and you would withhold moxa from the one patient who most needs it. The difference is one word — cold — and it changes the technique. 若然，則治法無別，而最需灸者反不與之。其別只在一「寒」字，而手法因之而異。"},{"t":"Yang deficiency is more severe qi deficiency","c":"陽虛者，氣虛之尤甚者","ok":0,"note":"Severity is not the axis. A profoundly qi-deficient patient can be quite warm; a mildly yang-deficient one is cold from the first week. Degree does not turn one into the other — the presence of cold does. 輕重非其軸。氣虛之甚者可不畏寒；陽虛之輕者，初起即冷。非由淺深而轉，乃由寒之有無而分。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"KI3","t":"T&#224;ix&#299; KI3 太谿","ok":1,"note":"Source point of the Kidney and its Stream point — the point for the Kidney organ itself, in either direction. Uniquely, it serves both Kidney yin and Kidney yang, because the Source point restores what the organ is short of. Moxa it here and it warms. 腎之原穴、輸穴，直治本臟，陰陽兩用。原穴補其所虧，故陰虛陽虛皆可取。本案加灸則溫。"},{"id":"ST36","t":"Z&#250;s&#257;nl&#464; ST36 足三里","ok":1,"note":"The acquired root feeding the innate one. The Kidney holds the qi we are born with and cannot be refilled directly; the Spleen and Stomach make qi daily from food, and that surplus is what banks the Kidney. It is also the point classically moxaed for long life in exactly this kind of patient. 以後天養先天。腎藏先天之精，不可徑補；脾胃日化水穀之氣，其餘乃歸於腎。此穴亦古來灸以延年者，正為此等人而設。"},{"id":"SP6","t":"S&#257;ny&#299;nji&#257;o SP6 三陰交","ok":1,"note":"Where the Spleen, Liver and Kidney channels cross — one needle reaching the Kidney and the Spleen together, which is precisely the pair at fault in dawn diarrhoea. With moxa it warms the middle and the lower burner at once. 足三陰交會之處，一針而腎脾俱及，正合五更瀉之病機。加灸則中下二焦同溫。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Y&#299;nl&#237;ngqu&#225;n SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"Drains damp from the lower burner. There is water here, but it is pooling because there is no fire to move it — drain it and you take fluid from a man who is already cold and empty. Warm the fire and the water moves itself. 利下焦之濕。本案水停，因無火以運，非因水盛。瀉之則奪其津，而其人本寒且虛。火復則水自行。"},{"id":"LU10","t":"Y&#250;j&#236; LU10 魚際","ok":0,"note":"Spring point of the Lung — it clears heat. There is no heat anywhere in this case, and cooling a man whose fire has burned low is the most direct way to make him worse. 肺經滎穴，主清熱。本案通身無熱。火將熄而更清之，害之最速者也。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"T&#224;ich&#333;ng LR3 太衝","ok":0,"note":"Soothes the Liver and moves qi. His stillness is emptiness, not constraint — and strong qi-moving disperses the little yang he has. Read the quality of the low mood: constrained is restless, empty is banked. 疏肝行氣。其靜為虛而非鬱；強行其氣，則散其僅存之陽。當辨情志之質：鬱者躁，虛者靜。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method, with generous moxa","c":"補法，重用灸","ok":1,"note":"Correct — and after four patients in which moxa was the wrong answer, this is the one that asks for it. Moxa warms and supplements yang; it is exactly what an empty hearth needs. Withhold it when there is heat (the ferryman), when there is dryness (the kiln-worker), and when a full pathogen is still lodged. Give it when the pattern is empty <b>and</b> cold. Needle retention can be a little longer here, and the needling gentle. 是。歷四案而灸皆非，至此乃為正法。灸能溫陽補虛，正合爐冷之證。有熱者忌（船家）、有燥者忌（窯場）、邪實未去者忌。虛而兼寒，乃其所宜。此案留針可稍久，手法宜輕。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, but no moxa","c":"補法，不施灸","ok":0,"note":"You have learned caution well — but caution applied everywhere stops being judgement. Moxa is withheld for heat, dryness or a lodged pathogen. This man has none of the three and cold in all of them. 慎已學得，然處處皆慎，則非權衡。忌灸者為熱、為燥、為邪實。此人三者皆無，而通身皆寒。"},{"t":"Reducing method with moxa, to drive out the cold","c":"瀉法加灸，以散其寒","ok":0,"note":"The moxa is right and the technique is wrong — this is the treatment for <b>full</b> cold, where a pathogen must be pushed out. Here there is no pathogen to expel. Drain an empty patient and you take away the very yang you are trying to build. 灸是而法非。此為實寒之治，邪當散之。本案無邪可散。虛而瀉之，適奪其所欲建之陽。"},{"t":"Even method, and warm herbs instead of moxa","c":"平補平瀉，以溫藥代灸","ok":0,"note":"Warm herbs certainly belong in the formula — but this is the needle room, and an even technique in a wholly deficient patient is a decision not to decide. When the entire case is empty, reinforce. 溫藥誠當入方，然此為針室；通案皆虛而用平補平瀉，是不決之決。全案屬虛者，補之。"}]};
